---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Code of conduct';
const description = `How we keep ${site.name} welcoming, and how to report a problem.`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Code of conduct</h1>

    <p class="prose__lede">
      Everyone should be able to turn up, ask a beginner question and go home having learned
      something. This page sets out what that requires of all of us.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Be decent to each other. Assume good faith. Leave people better off than you found
      them.
    </p>

    <h2>Expected behaviour</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Be respectful and considerate in talks, questions, chat and hallway conversation.</li>
      <li>
        Remember that experience levels vary enormously. There are no stupid questions at
        this meetup.
      </li>
      <li>Give feedback on ideas and code, not on people.</li>
      <li>Respect the venue, its staff and its rules.</li>
      <li>Ask before photographing or recording someone, and respect a "no".</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Unacceptable behaviour</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Harassment or discrimination based on gender, gender identity or expression, sexual
        orientation, disability, neurotype, physical appearance, body size, race, ethnicity,
        nationality, age, religion, or experience level.
      </li>
      <li>Sexual language or imagery, and unwelcome sexual attention of any kind.</li>
      <li>Deliberate intimidation, stalking, or following.</li>
      <li>Sustained disruption of talks or other events.</li>
      <li>Publishing others' private information without explicit permission.</li>
      <li>Recruiting or selling to attendees who have not invited it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reporting</h2>
    <p>
      If you experience or witness anything that breaks this code — or anything that just
      feels off — tell an organiser. We are the people wearing the group's badge, and we would
      much rather hear about something small than find out later it became something large.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also email us at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      Reports go only to the organiser team, and we will not share your identity with the
      person reported without your agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>
      Organisers will listen, take the report seriously, and decide on a response. Depending
      on the severity that may be a quiet word, a request to stop, removal from the event, or
      a ban from future events. Where a venue's own policies apply, or where someone is in
      danger, we will involve venue staff or emergency services.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This code applies at our meetups and social events, and in any online space the group
      runs — Meetup comments, LinkedIn, chat and our YouTube channel included.
    </p>

    <h2>Credit</h2>
    <p>
      Adapted from the
      <a href="https://www.contributor-covenant.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Contributor Covenant
      </a>
      and the
      <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/developer/community/community-builders/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        AWS Community
      </a>
      guidelines. Reuse it freely.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
